  "details": "Since the latest update (Build 1885), you can no longer send a Request Invite to a friend who is in a joinable instance (Friends / Friends+) — only \"Join\" is shown.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Have a friend join a Friends or Friends+ instance (an instance you are able to join)\n\n2. Open their user detail page from the Social menu\n\n3. Look for the \"Request Invite\" option\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n\"Request Invite\" is available alongside \"Join\", as in previous builds.\n\n## Actual Behavior\n\nOnly \"Join\" is available. There is no way to send a Request Invite.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nEven when an instance is technically joinable, many users send a Request Invite first to ask \"is now a good time to join?\" instead of jumping in directly. This usage is especially well-established in the Japanese community.\n\nThe friend may be in the middle of a conversation, an event, or taking photos. There are many situations where you want to check whether it's okay to join right now — for example, to avoid running into someone you'd rather not meet who happens to be in the same instance.\n\nPlease bring back the ability to send Request Invites in this situation.",
